---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const guide = {
  "title": "Umrah from Pakistan: Visa Routes, Nusuk & Travel Checks",
  "description": "Plan Umrah through official services, separating visa conditions, permits, package costs and current seasonal health requirements.",
  "intro": "Plan Umrah through official services, separating visa conditions, permits, package costs and current seasonal health requirements.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Official Nusuk Umrah platform",
      "url": "https://umrah.nusuk.sa/"
    },
    {
      "title": "Saudi July 2026 visa announcement",
      "url": "https://pep.gov.sa/en/news/1004"
    },
    {
      "title": "Saudi Ministry of Health pilgrim guidance",
      "url": "https://www.moh.gov.sa/en/healthawareness/pilgrims-health/pages/default.aspx"
    },
    {
      "title": "Saudi visa service",
      "url": "https://ksavisa.sa/"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Check the eligible route",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Use Nusuk and the visa service for nationality, residence and travel dates. Do not assume Pakistanis are universally excluded from direct online services, or that every Pakistani qualifies for tourist or transit permission. A package purchase is not a visa approval."
      ],
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "heading": "Read the 2026 update",
      "paragraphs": [
        "A government announcement of 20 July 2026 describes a 365-day multiple-entry Umrah visa with a cumulative stay of up to 90 days, subject to package, permit, reactivation and Hajj-season conditions. Do not apply those terms to every existing visa; read the issued permission."
      ],
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "Compare actual package contents",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Nusuk is supervised by the Ministry of Hajj and Umrah and lists accredited providers. Compare what is included: visa services, flights, hotel nights, occupancy, meals, transfers and permits. Headline prices can describe very different arrangements.",
        "Get hotel names, dates, transport arrangements, cancellation terms and provider contact details in writing. Verify the provider through the official channel. Save receipts and confirmations, and check what happens if travel dates or visa availability change."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Check health and family requirements",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Use the Ministry of Health’s current pilgrim guidance for the travel season and origin. Confirm vaccinations and timing with a qualified health provider. Do not rely on an old fixed vaccine-validity period or a blanket age/child rule from another season."
      ],
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "heading": "Before departure",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Confirm entry deadline, stay period, entries, required permits, accommodation and transport. Seasonal restrictions matter even where ordinary permission is valid. Carry confirmations and an emergency contact plan. Umrah permission is not permission for Hajj or ordinary employment."
      ],
      "source": 3
    }
  ]
};
---
<GuideLayout {...guide} />
